{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c88a-6674-7861-9d70-d3e79e98c472"},"sequence":325,"recorded_at":1780531400000645,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c88b-198a-7462-8a5c-75b50007365d"},"task_id":"01a0c88b-198a-7462-8a5c-75b50007365d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c88b-198a-7462-8a5c-75b50007365d","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev5_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1c28dz rework rev5 — results (standalone)\n2|\n3|Ready for review. This run repairs the rev4 CHANGES REQUESTED on\n4|checkpoint `d4bd91d0` (trunk unmoved, no rebase). Both P1 close by\n5|construction rather than by case analysis; P2-A, P2-B, and P3 close\n6|with the requested instruments. The worktree is intentionally\n7|UNCOMMITTED for the Story handoff snapshot.\n8|\n9|Scope of the production delta (all in `internal/tmuxserver`):\n10|`state.go` (incarnation store + incarnation-scoped barrier scan),\n11|`lifecycle.go` (incarnation binding, failure recording, create\n12|rotation), `ops.go` (proof-only admission + health check, restore\n13|rotation), `wrapper.go` (composed binding). Touched landed files:\n14|error-code registry (new codes, prior revision), ownership seam\n15|(test hook, prior revision), mutant harnesses (new rows). No other\n16|production file changed.\n17|\n18|## P1-A — the barrier verdict is the incarnation-scoped proof alone\n19|\n20|Construction: every closure report binds the incarnation that was\n21|current when it recorded; a fresh create or restore success rotates\n22|the incarnation to its own idempotency key; replays never rotate;\n23|the attach entry consults exactly `QuiesceBarrierProven` (plus a\n24|store-health read whose value is ignored and whose error fails\n25|closed). Advisory memory, caller-carried source state, and failure\n26|reporting cannot reopen a closed barrier because admission never\n27|reads their values; a new incarnation supersedes stale reports\n28|because the scan skips them. Row 79's lost-write claim now reads\n29|as the construction (memory is advisory; the proof decides).\n30|\n31|Writer census — every writer of barrier-relevant state:\n32|\n33|| # | Writer (file:function) | What it writes | Proof the barrier holds |\n34||---|---|---|---|\n35|| W1 | lifecycle.go:executeCreate success | best-effort Active/Parked memory; checked incarnation rotation on fresh success only | `TestExecuteCreateReplayPreservesBarrier` (replay skips) + `TestExecuteCreateIncarnationWriteFailureFailsClosed` (lost rotation fails closed); memory values proven ignored by `TestExecuteAdvisoryMemoryNeverDecidesAdmission` |\n36|| W2 | lifecycle.go:executeEngineOp non-barrier success | best-effort memory (stop) | `TestExecuteStop` memory pin; values ignored for admission (same advisory test) |\n37|| W3 | lifecycle.go:executeEngineOp barrier success | checked memory (status fidelity) + closure report binding the current incarnation | `TestExecuteAttachRefusesInputWhenQuiescing` + `N-quiesce-state-record` / `N-boundary-state-record` |\n38|| W4 | lifecycle.go:recordFailure | first echo only when absent; honest unknown overwrites | `TestReviewFailedStopCannotEraseQuiescence` + `N-failure-preserves-record` (never-overwrite); `TestExecuteTerminateResumesAfterEffectFailure` (first-echo resume) |\n39|| W5 | ops.go:executeAttach success | best-effort active memory | `TestExecuteAttach` memory pin; values ignored for admission (same advisory test) |\n40|| W6 | ops.go:runLifecycleEffects success | best-effort target memory; checked incarnation rotation on fresh restore only | `TestExecuteRestoreReplayPreservesBarrier` + `D-restore-replay-rotation` (structural, B41); `TestExecuteTerminate` + `N-terminate-no-rotation` (terminate never rotates) |\n41|| W7 | state.go:RecordOutcome via report funcs | closure report + incarnation bind, first success records, retries replay | `TestExecuteQuiesceRetryAfterStateWriteFailureHealsBarrier` (+ boundary twin); `N-quiesce-report-record` / `N-boundary-report-record` |\n42|\n43|Reader census — every reader deciding admission:\n44|\n45|| # | Reader (file:function) | What it trusts | Proof / bound |\n46||---|---|---|---|\n47|| R1 | ops.go:checkAttachQuiesced | the incarnation-scoped closure proof as the sole verdict | `TestExecuteAdvisoryMemoryNeverDecidesAdmission` forces memory both directions with no verdict change; `N-quiesce-attach-gate` (re-anchored to the proof) |\n48|| R2 | ops.go:checkAttachQuiesced health read | nothing (value ignored); read errors propagate | `TestExecuteAttachErrorsOnStateReadFailure` + `N-attach-health-check`; the Lookup absent arm itself is `N-state-read-absent` |\n49|| R3 | state.go:QuiesceBarrierProven scoping | current incarnation; stale reports skipped | `TestExecuteQuiesceStopRestoreReopensBarrier` + `N-attach-barrier-incarnation`; store-level `TestQuiesceBarrierIgnoresSupersededIncarnation` |\n50|| R4 | status.go:ClassifyStatus memory leg | advisory memory for status only, never admission | status rows 80/88; the reopen test admits attach while stale reports persist, proving the split |\n51|\n52|The two reviewer sequences run verbatim:\n53|`TestReviewExistingActiveMemoryCannotReopenQuiescedInput` (stale\n54|active + lost state write refuses via the proof) and\n55|`TestReviewFailedStopCannotEraseQuiescence` (failed stop preserves\n56|quiescing memory and refuses). The legitimate reopening is\n57|`TestExecuteQuiesceStopRestoreReopensBarrier` (quiesce→stop→\n58|restore→writable attach admitted, incarnation asserted).\n59|\n60|Bound B40 (owner: axpane receipt/bootstrap contracts): a lost\n61|rotation with a prior closure stays closed with no\n62|production-entry recovery — retries replay without rotating, and a\n63|fresh key is unreachable (one bootstrap per session, pinned\n64|mechanically in\n65|`TestExecuteCreateIncarnationWriteFailureFailsClosed` via the\n66|landed `idempotency_mismatch`). Over-strict in the safe direction;\n67|a lost rotation with no prior closure is harmless (self-consistent\n68|zero incarnation). Bound B41 (owner: this leaf): the restore\n69|replay skip is structural (no code to narrow); the supplementary\n70|`D-restore-replay-rotation` proves the test observes the forbidden\n71|write.\n72|\n73|## P1-B — one composed authorization over six members\n74|\n75|`checkRestoreComposedBound` (wrapper.go) refuses\n76|`local_precondition_failed` before any effect unless the executed\n77|restore names the decided session, bootstrap, admitted-descriptor\n78|instance/backend/generation triple, and winner lease/epoch. The\n79|descriptor triple comes from the landed\n80|`terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor` output inside Decide —\n81|compared, never re-parsed.\n82|\n83|Identity census — every identity member the decision and the\n84|effect each carry:\n85|\n86|| # | Decision member | Effect member | Disposition |\n87||---|---|---|---|\n88|| 1 | Decide.SessionID | mctx.SessionID | JOINED — `TestWrapperRestoreRefusesDivergentSession` + `N-wrapper-restore-session` |\n89|| 2 | Decide.BootstrapOperationID | body.BootstrapOperationID | JOINED — `TestReviewWrapperBootstrapMustBindExecutedRestore` + `N-wrapper-restore-bootstrap` |\n90|| 3 | admitted Descriptor.TerminalInstanceID | mctx.TerminalInstanceID | JOINED — `TestReviewWrapperInstanceMustBindExecutedRestore` + `N-wrapper-restore-instance` |\n91|| 4 | admitted Descriptor.TerminalBackendID | mctx.TerminalBackendID | JOINED — `TestWrapperRestoreRefusesDivergentBackend` + `N-wrapper-restore-backend` |\n92|| 5 | admitted Descriptor.BackendGeneration | mctx.BackendGeneration | JOINED — `TestWrapperRestoreRefusesDivergentGeneration` + `N-wrapper-restore-generation` |\n93|| 6 | ordered winner (lease_id, epoch) | auth (lease_id, epoch) | JOINED — rev4 tests + `N-wrapper-winner-lease`, `N-wrapper-winner-epoch` (kept) |\n94|| 7 | winner HolderHostID | auth holder_host_id | UNJOINED — backend `CheckAuthorization` binds kind/expiry/lease/epoch only (terminstance/auth.go); the holder routes inside Decide's fencing arm |\n95|| 8 | Journal/materialization | (no counterpart) | UNJOINED — decision-local gate enforced inside Decide before effects; restore carries no materialization member |\n96|| 9 | checkpoint (Newest/Required) | body.CheckpointID | UNJOINED — different roles: decision admission runs over the fold authority; the restore checkpoint is opaque carried evidence with no production consumer (bodies.go only) |\n97|| 10 | ExistingBinding | body.PriorBindingID | UNJOINED — backend `checkPriorBinding` binds the prior to the recorded receipt; the decision binding drives the bootstrap-window verdict |\n98|| 11 | descriptor versions (provider build) | mctx versions (AX API) | UNJOINED — different namespaces; the honest fixture differs by design (2.1.0/1.1.0 vs 1.2.3/1.0.0) |\n99|| 12 | descriptor TerminalBindingID | body.PriorBindingID | UNJOINED — different namespaces (host-local provider binding vs recorded bootstrap binding; honest differs) |\n100|| 13 | Presented/Observation/Entrypoint/Profile/Provider/Realm/Backend-facts | (no counterpart) | N/A — decision-local inputs enforced inside Decide |\n101|\n102|Table E grows 17→22 outcomes with the five composed-binding\n103|refusals, each with a divergence test asserting the wrapper\n104|detail, a launched decision, zero backend outcome, and zero\n105|executed subcommands.\n106|\n107|## P2-B — the four clause gaps, all witnessed\n108|\n109|| Gap | Committed test (production entry) | Harness row (reviewer plant shape) |\n110||---|---|---|\n111|| R1 malformed attached count `0junk` | `TestExecuteStatusMalformedAttachedCountIsUnknown` via `Execute(status)` | `N-status-attached-parse` — admits exactly `0junk` past the parse-error clause |\n112|| R2 exactly-`{}` barrier report | `TestExecuteAttachErrorsOnEmptyBarrierKey` via `Execute(attach)` | `N-attach-barrier-empty-key` — admits exactly `{}` past the empty-key arm |\n113|| R3 prober writable-root custody | `TestServerProberRefusesWritableRoot` via `ServerProber.Probe` | `N-prober-root-custody` — admits exactly the writable-root class; the PRB rootwrite cell moves B39→M |\n114|| R4 EISDIR state-read failure | `TestExecuteAttachErrorsOnStateReadFailure` via `Execute(attach)` | `N-state-read-absent` — admits exactly EISDIR as absence |\n115|\n116|## P2-A — closure outcome grid (36-package variant, declared)\n117|\n118|The fixed-corpus driver `closuregrid` (ships in the evidence\n119|tarball, copied into each tree; no clock, no randomness, no\n120|network; filesystem probes normalized to `<tmp>`) records\n121|`(package, entry, input class) -> (outcome, refusal string,\n122|value summary)` over the reviewer's 36-package closure\n123|(34 production + crashgate + environ). 33 packages probed;\n124|3 stated bounds with owners (no exported pure callable\n125|surface; fenced by the suite-verdict grid below): cloneproject,\n126|crashgate, sshtransport. The 7 tmuxserver records for\n127|story-added entries sit behind the `closuregrid_candidate`\n128|build tag and are declared candidate-only by construction.\n129|\n130|- Shared keys: 193. MOVED: 0. Base-only: 0.\n131|- Candidate-only: 7, all declared (`tmuxserver/CheckSocketLength`\n132|  × short/long, `tmuxserver/ClassifyStatus` × 5 input classes).\n133|- Stability: 6/6 identical candidate runs (sha256 match). One\n134|  flake found and fixed during authoring (resumesmoke's\n135|  missing-member loop iterates a map; the inputs now fail\n136|  deterministically before it), and every member-naming error in\n137|  the corpus audited for fixed-order checks (clonebundle,\n138|  canonicaljson, sessrepo) or member-free strings (provhost,\n139|  termbind).\n140|- Suite verdicts over the complete importer set: 23,874 shared\n141|  `(package, test)` keys, zero moved verdicts, zero base-only,\n142|  498 candidate-only additions (493 tmuxserver incl. subtests,\n143|  5 termbind), all PASS. No input moved across any admission or\n144|  refusal arm: the outcome grid above names every probed input\n145|  and every one is identical or declared.\n146|\n147|## P3 — prose\n148|\n149|B27 counts 18 U2c cells (was 19). The determinism sentence now\n150|reads \"no committed test execs a real tmux or dials a real tmux\n151|server socket (one dialer test dials a synthetic local listener\n152|it creates itself, not a tmux server)\" in the matrix, results\n153|narrative, and README-adjacent claims.\n154|\n155|## Census and ratios\n156|\n157|- Gate × entry census (Tables A/B/D recomputed by script over\n158|  the tables): 250 measured of 5064 (50+10+190 M); 187 bound;\n159|  4627 unreachable with reasons; 156 named undriven gaps (148\n160|  B39 + 8 named cells; B40/B41 are non-cell bounds). Table C\n161|  all U. Every two-sided gate carries a row-count symmetry line\n162|  (rotation create 1 / restore 1; custody CUS 1 / EXC 1 / EXS 1 /\n163|  EXR 1 / PRB 1 / SPW 1 + shared row; reached-lookup EXA 1 /\n164|  LOOK 2 on different arms).\n165|- AC rows 59-92: 34 of 34 driven through production entries by\n166|  named tests (call sites in the matrix).\n167|- Eight operations, 8 of 8, each through `Lifecycle.Execute`\n168|  (lifecycle.go) by a named committed test: create\n169|  (`TestExecuteCreateInteractive`), attach (`TestExecuteAttach`),\n170|  status (`TestExecuteStatusPresent`), quiesce\n171|  (`TestExecuteQuiesce`), safe-boundary (`TestExecuteBoundary`),\n172|  stop (`TestExecuteStop`), stale termination\n173|  (`TestExecuteTerminate`), restore (`TestExecuteRestore`).\n174|- Mutant battery: 273/273 tmuxserver rows as expected (269\n175|  narrowing `N-*` + 3 additive `D-*` KILLED, shared control\n176|  SURVIVED), 40/40 termbind rows as expected; one raw log per\n177|  plant in the tarball. 22 new tmuxserver rows this round (21\n178|  narrowing + 1 supplementary), 4 re-anchored to the\n179|  construction (attach gate, failure record, two report\n180|  records, state foreign split).\n181|- No-real-tmux: zero real-tmux witnesses by the determinism\n182|  design (bound B1); tmux is installed on this host and no tmux\n183|  process ran before, during, or after the suite (pgrep audit\n184|  in the evidence).\n185|\n186|## Validation (all exit 0, this run)\n187|\n188|| Gate | Result |\n189||---|---|\n190|| `go test ./... -count=1` candidate / base | 45 ok / 45 ok |\n191|| `go test -race` tmuxserver + termbind | ok, no races |\n192|| `go test ./... -cover` | ok (tmuxserver 88.0%, termbind 83.5%) |\n193|| `go vet ./...` + `GOOS=windows go vet` touched pkgs | clean |\n194|| `gofmt -l internal/` | clean |\n195|| tmuxserver harness 273 + termbind harness 40 | all as expected |\n196|| no-tmux process audit | no tmux process before/after; suite green |\n197|| closure grid determinism | 6/6 identical streams |\n198|| census recount + matrix mirror check | counts match; AC/census/bounds byte-identical |\n199|\n200|## Evidence\n201|\n202|- `TASK-260830-1c28dz_conformance-matrix.md` (updated, attached):\n203|  AC rows, ops table, mirrored census Tables B/C/D + Table E,\n204|  bounds B22-B41, battery, crash/idempotency.\n205|- `TASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-evidence-rev5.tar.gz` (attached):\n206|  closure grid driver + base/candidate streams + diff,\n207|  per-test verdict streams + diff, full suite logs both trees,\n208|  273 + 40 raw per-plant harness logs, vet/fmt/race/cover/\n209|  no-tmux logs, census recount, mirror check, SHA256SUMS.\n210|- Handoff: ready for review; candidate UNCOMMITTED in the\n211|  Story worktree for snapshot.","final_result":true}}}
