{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e2e3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c88a-6674-7861-9d70-d3e79e98c472"},"sequence":4044,"recorded_at":1780531400008083,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c8a7-1832-7f73-b193-8cf472157d88"},"task_id":"01a0c8a7-1832-7f73-b193-8cf472157d88","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c8a7-1832-7f73-b193-8cf472157d88","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-106-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board spawn directives \\\"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\\\" 2>&1 | head -c 1000; echo; head -n 30 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check directives and LOGBOOK head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"Active Goal: none (run is not goal-bound)\\nNo directives recorded for RUN-260922-6f89bb\\n\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### BUG-260917-3lddu0 — superseded leases are refused before append admission\\n\\n- FIX: `Repository.AppendEvent` now calls `checkWinningLease` after loading the durable lease winner and before `checkAppend`. Lower-epoch events refuse `ErrStaleLease`; same-epoch losing leases refuse `ErrDivergentBranch`. Refused branch bytes remain immutable and addressable, while the authoritative chain is unchanged. Historical replay intentionally does not apply this owner-side gate.\\n- REPRO: the exact trunk baseline at `799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2` was driven through an adapted production `AppendEvent` probe: a successor won while the tail still named A, then A's append returned `err=<nil>` and the negative expected stale refusal. The archived review probe 15 records the old blast radius verbatim: losing-lease `profile.changed` drove `profile=yolo` with mapping `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`. The candidate test `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored` now refuses the append and proves `Run` cannot use that source.\\n- AC: 2 of 2 leaf rows are driven. The gate × production-entry census is 8 of 10 cells: 4 lower-epoch and 4 same-epoch loser cells across `AppendEvent`, `SetProfile`, `Emit`, and `EmitParked`; both `Run → EmitParked` cells are bounded as unreachable except by an interleaving between `Observe` and `AppendEvent`, closed by the durable gate. Row symmetry is 4/4 versus 4/4. `N-stale-winning-admission` and `N-same-epoch-winning-admission` retain the gate, admit one reachable rejected class each, and are KILLED twice; controls are classified separately.\\n- LANDED-TEST MEANING TABLE: the name-keyed outcome grid cannot expose four stable-name input changes. `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes`, `TestRunSupersededPairIdenticalRetry`, and `TestRunCreateFromStoppedPostWindow` now publish `session.idle` + `session.stopped` under A before successor B; the old successor-first fixture would move those A-after-B stop events to literal `ErrStaleLease`. `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored` changed from admitting lower-epoch `profile.changed` and checking downstream Run into asserting raw `AppendEvent` refusal; its before outcome was yolo with `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`. The full table and §5.2/§5.3 or §2.4 citations are in the task results and axpane TRACEABILITY.\\n\\n| Stable-name test | Moved input / meaning | Spec |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes`; `TestRunSupersededPairIdenticalRetry`; `TestRunCreateFromStoppedPostWindow` | A-owned `session.idle` + `session.stopped` after B would now be `ErrStaleLease`; each fixture now publishes before B. | §5.2/§5.3 |\\n| `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored` | A-owned lower-epoch `profile.changed` after B was admitted/yolo before; now raw `AppendEvent` refuses and preserves it, so profile stays standard/no source. | §2.4 + §5.3 |\\n- IMPORTER DIFF: complete importer mask is `./internal/axpane ./internal/crashgate ./internal/fencing ./internal/sessckpt ./internal/sessprofile ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessstate ./internal/termbind ./internal/terminstance`. The old comparison is a test-status grid: 2,018/2,030 keys including 9 package rows, or 2,009/2,021 actual test rows; 12 named additions, 0 removed, 0 changed statuses; all 9 package summaries PASS. It is not runtime admission evidence. The adopted reviewer runtime grid over the same nine-package importer set records 130 outcome keys / 2,926 calls before versus 137 / 2,955 after, with 10 added and 3 removed outcome keys; every moved arm is named in the results and matrix. Direct sessrepo tests are outside the importer mask and named in the matrix.\\n- TRACEABILITY: route (b) owns the losing-profile registry case at `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo.go:AppendEvent`; independent lease-aware derivation-side authority is a bound owned by `STORY-260922-cpkajd` / `TASK-260922-31qyyi`, not an independent guarantee in this leaf. The case is referenced by Section 2.4 clause 2.4#2. Candidate registry digest is re-derived after that edge as `174728a8a01e8429004e4f9c4687f8fa1f17406b641012236c3427a758baf31e`; exact-tree tracecheck prints `contracts=64 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=154 fixtures=33 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0` and `section coverage: bindings=69 full=4 partial=9 sliver=9 unevidenced=43 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=70/574`. Section 2.4 admits; section 5.3 correctly refuses assigned-scope admission at 7/8 partial coverage.\\n- P3 DISPOSITIONS: the axpane `decide.go` “lapsed grants refuse” qualifier remains untouched and is scoped to the local-owner path; `observeRemoteWinner` structural redundancy is record-only; the grant-less remote interactive-owner step-4 product question remains unresolved and undecided; unknown higher epoch and empty lease-store behavior are named bounds with owners; evidence records the final candidate TREE OID in the task matrix and keeps the exact test masks beside every row count.\\n- MUTATION: the shipped harness ran twice under `mutants-append-rev3-pass1/` and `mutants-append-rev3-pass2/`. Both true reachable narrowings are KILLED twice; comment controls SURVIVE, missing-token controls are NOT_APPLIED, syntax controls are COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE, and control-before/after suites exit 0. Raw per-plant logs and exits are retained in both directories.\\n- VALIDATION: the fresh configured run is recorded under `.temp/BUG-260917-3lddu0/validation-rev3/`; all 30 configured commands exited 0. `task-board validate` reported 179 existing `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics and exited 0; scoped tracecheck §2.4 exited 0 and §5.3 exited 1 as the expected 7/8 refusal.\\n- HANDOFF: importer outcomes and tracecheck logs are task-scoped; the candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for snapshot handoff.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz — tmux lifecycle operations via structured commands (initial producer delivery)\\n\\n- SHIPPED the second `tmuxserver` leaf: `Execute` admits exactly the eight lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, restore) and refuses unknown ones; the exec adapter reconstructs the exact `tmux -S <socket> <subcommand>` vector per operation (forged binaries, flag injection, ambient discovery all refuse); the probed socket generation binds before execution (B18-B20); bodies are pure argv builders with the stable `ax pane SESSION_ID` entrypoint; effects run through the landed terminstance engine with strict per-operation deadlines, generation rechecks, and AX-side state memory, while attach/terminate/restore mirror the landed backend/fencing/axpane gates. Every mutating operation replays idempotently; uncertain receipts reconcile through status before resuming.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6961,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1741,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
