{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e30f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c88a-6674-7861-9d70-d3e79e98c472"},"sequence":4066,"recorded_at":1780531400008127,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c8a7-4627-7853-94fe-f1caa280c4ef"},"task_id":"01a0c8a7-4627-7853-94fe-f1caa280c4ef","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c8a7-4627-7853-94fe-f1caa280c4ef","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-22\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-22\n+\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev6 — attach/quiesce ordering contract; closure-authority escalation\n+\n+- P1-B FIXED: attach now revalidates the quiesce barrier under `Lifecycle.barrierMu` immediately before committing its writable client receipt, holding the lock through the receipt, the returned vector, and the advisory memory record; quiesce holds the same lock across engine closure plus report commit, boundary across its report commit only (the wait blocks on the wrapper signal). Contract: report commits and receipt commits are mutually exclusive, whichever lands first wins, no writable receipt commits after a durable closure report. Three committed tests: paused-admission late attach refuses, plus quiesce/boundary overlap tests that launch attach from inside the report write via the state crash seam and assert it blocks then refuses. Narrowings `N-attach-barrier-recheck` and `N-ordering-lock-{attach,quiesce,boundary}` (instance-scoped) all KILLED; symmetry attach 1 / quiesce 1 / boundary 1.\n+- P1-A ESCALATED (structural, not a fourth guard): a lost outcome-report write after committed engine closure still admits a fresh writable attach until retry heals the report, because admission consults the outcome proof alone and pending-vs-committed is unrepresentable there. Bound B43 names owner `internal/terminstance ReceiptStore` and the scoped contract (completed-closure enumeration distinguishing pending-without-completion from completed); row 79 now claims only the lost state-record write fails closed. Same window covers receipt/report crash and double loss. B42 states the in-process bound on the ordering lock (cross-process needs a lock file) and that the covered vector handoff ends at construction.\n+- P2-A CLOSED: three read-error arms now fail closed through `Execute(attach)` with tests plus reviewer-shaped narrowings — incarnation EISDIR-as-absence (`N-incarnation-read-absent`), outcomes ENOTDIR-as-absence (`N-outcomes-dir-read-absent`), outcome-file EISDIR skip via `.json`-symlink-to-dir (`N-outcome-file-read-skip`) — and the attach entry of the unsafe-root gate carries its own valid-body test plus `N-attach-entry-root-custody` (weakened attach is served, proving admission rather than rerouting).\n+- P2-B CLOSED: importer outcome corpus now covers 36/36 packages (198 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 7 declared candidate-only; 6/6 stable runs) with `cloneproject.Normalize` no-fetcher/no-sink refusals, `sshtransport.New(zero)` invalid-snapshot refusal, and `crashgate.Lookup` known/unknown rows. Suite-verdict grid: 23,874 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 505 candidate-only additions, 0 fails.\n+- P3 CLOSED: Table C recounted from the Table D gate set (140 gates × 11 = 1540; total census 255 measured of 5248 with 186 bounds and 4807 unreachable, verified by script); row 72 lease-members prose corrected to the ownership-neutral authorization; README quiesce claim narrowed to report-committed refusal plus B43; battery counts updated (281 tmuxserver rows: 277 narrowing + 3 supplementary + control).\n+- PROCESS: an overlap test that consumes the attach result inside the hook then re-waits on the same channel hangs 10s under the lock-removal plant; putting the result back keeps the kill fast with two failure lines. Copying the outcome-grid driver into a tree breaks `go test ./...` via the specdoc no-product-command gate — run the driver, remove the directory, then run the suite.\n+\n+## 2026-09-22\n","final_result":true}}}
