 after committed engine closure still admits a fresh writable attach until retry heals the report, because admission consults the outcome proof alone and pending-vs-committed is unrepresentable there. Bound B43 names owner `internal/terminstance ReceiptStore` and the scoped contract (completed-closure enumeration distinguishing pending-without-completion from completed); row 79 now claims only the lost state-record write fails closed. Same window covers receipt/report crash and double loss. B42 states the in-process bound on the ordering lock (cross-process needs a lock file) and that the covered vector handoff ends at construction.\n+- P2-A CLOSED: three read-error arms now fail closed through `Execute(attach)` with tests plus reviewer-shaped narrowings — incarnation EISDIR-as-absence (`N-incarnation-read-absent`), outcomes ENOTDIR-as-absence (`N-outcomes-dir-read-absent`), outcome-file EISDIR skip via `.json`-symlink-to-dir (`N-outcome-file-read-skip`) — and the attach entry of the unsafe-root gate carries its own valid-body test plus `N-attach-entry-root-custody` (weakened attach is served, proving admission rather than rerouting).\n+- P2-B CLOSED: importer outcome corpus now covers 36/36 packages (198 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 7 declared candidate-only; 6/6 stable runs) with `cloneproject.Normalize` no-fetcher/no-sink refusals, `sshtransport.New(zero)` invalid-snapshot refusal, and `crashgate.Lookup` known/unknown rows. Suite-verdict grid: 23,874 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 505 candidate-only additions, 0 fails.\n+- P3 CLOSED: Table C recounted from the Table D gate set (140 gates × 11 = 1540; total census 255 measured of 5248 with 186 bounds and 4807 unreachable, verified by script); row 72 lease-members prose corrected to the ownership-neutral authorization; README quiesce claim narrowed to report-committed refusal plus B43; battery counts updated (281 tmuxserver rows: 277 narrowing + 3 supplementary + control).\n+- PROCESS: an overlap test that consumes the attach result inside the hook then re-waits on the same channel hangs 10s under the lock-removal plant; putting the result back keeps the kill fast with two failure lines. Copying the outcome-grid driver into a tree breaks `go test ./...` via the specdoc no-product-command gate — run the driver, remove the directory, then run the suite.\n+\n+## 2026-09-22\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"LOGBOOK.md","added":17,"removed":6},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
