{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e941","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c88a-6674-7861-9d70-d3e79e98c472"},"sequence":4859,"recorded_at":1780531400009713,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"995ec337-5e4d-4fd4-a64e-ae914055ec56"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c8b9-137a-75c1-8402-ab5b5e603b1b"},"task_id":"01a0c8b9-137a-75c1-8402-ab5b5e603b1b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c8b9-137a-75c1-8402-ab5b5e603b1b","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev6_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1c28dz rework rev6 — results (standalone)\n2|\n3|Ready for review. This run answers the rev5 CHANGES REQUESTED on\n4|checkpoint `d4bd91d0` (trunk unmoved, no rebase): P1-B, P2-A, P2-B\n5|and P3 close with instruments; P1-A is escalated as the structural\n6|receipt-owner contract the brief explicitly accepts as a complete\n7|revision 6, with its boundary stated and every P1-A-adjacent claim\n8|narrowed to match. The worktree is intentionally UNCOMMITTED for\n9|the Story handoff snapshot.\n10|\n11|Scope of the production delta (all in `internal/tmuxserver`):\n12|`lifecycle.go` (ordering-lock field, quiesce/boundary report\n13|spans), `ops.go` (authoritative attach recheck under the lock).\n14|No other production file changed. Touched landed files: none this\n15|round (error registry, ownership seam, and harnesses keep their\n16|prior-revision changes).\n17|\n18|## Finding-by-finding disposition\n19|\n20|| # | Verdict finding | Disposition | Witness |\n21||---|---|---|---|\n22|| P1-A | outcome-report write failure after committed closure reopens input (third boundary) | ESCALATED — bound B43: owner `internal/terminstance ReceiptStore`, scoped contract is completed-closure enumeration distinguishing pending-without-completion from completed; row 79 narrowed to the lost state-record write, B34 discloses reopening, README narrowed | B43 text in TRACEABILITY + matrix; no fourth guard added |\n23|| P1-B | in-flight attach commits after successful quiescence (logical check/use race, no data race) | FIXED — one ordering contract at the effect boundary: attach rechecks the barrier under `barrierMu` immediately before its receipt commit and holds it through receipt, returned vector, and memory; quiesce holds it across engine closure plus report, boundary across its report only | `TestAttachRefusesAfterQuiescenceWhenAdmittedLate`, `TestAttachQuiesceOrderingOverlapQuiesce`, `TestAttachQuiesceOrderingOverlapBoundary` via `Lifecycle.Execute`; narrowings `N-attach-barrier-recheck`, `N-ordering-lock-{attach,quiesce,boundary}` |\n24|| P2-A | three read-error narrowings survive (incarnation EISDIR, outcomes ENOTDIR, outcome-file EISDIR) | FIXED — three production-entry tests plus three reviewer-shaped narrowings; attach custody entry carries its own valid-body test plus narrowing | tests + `N-incarnation-read-absent`, `N-outcomes-dir-read-absent`, `N-outcome-file-read-skip`, `N-attach-entry-root-custody` |\n25|| P2-B | corpus excludes cloneproject, sshtransport, crashgate on a false premise | FIXED — five representative rows added; corpus covers 36/36 with no exclusion bounds | closure grid 198 shared keys, 0 moved; verdict grid 23,874 shared, 0 moved |\n26|| P3 | Table C denominator stale (129 vs 137 gates); attach \"lease members\" prose; README/row-79 overclaims | FIXED — Table C recounted from the Table D gate set (140 gates incl. 3 new); row 72 corrected; README + row 79 narrowed | recount script over both tables; mirror check TRACEABILITY vs matrix |\n27|\n28|## P1-A — escalation with the boundary (no fourth guard)\n29|\n30|Three boundaries in three rounds is structural: the barrier is\n31|reconstructed from whichever storage artefact survived, so the\n32|failure to create the outcome proof reads as permission. This\n33|revision does not add another guard. Bound B43 (in TRACEABILITY\n34|and mirrored in the matrix) states:\n35|\n36|- Owner: `internal/terminstance ReceiptStore` (landed receipt\n37|  owner). Scoped contract: completed-closure enumeration — the\n38|  completed quiesce/boundary receipts for one instance,\n39|  distinguishing pending-without-completion from completed — so\n40|  attach admission can consult receipt completion as the\n41|  authoritative proof with pending-versus-committed\n42|  representable. This leaf owns the admission side once it\n43|  lands.\n44|- Boundary: a lost outcome-report write after committed closure\n45|  admits a fresh writable attach until the identical retry heals\n46|  the report; the same window covers a crash between the receipt\n47|  commit and the report, and a simultaneous loss of both the\n48|  report and the state record. Retrying the identical quiesce\n49|  heals the report and re-closes input; no other production\n50|  entry heals it.\n51|\n52|Every P1-A-adjacent claim now matches the boundary: row 79\n53|claims only the lost state-record write fails closed (still\n54|proven by `TestExecuteQuiesceStateWriteFailureRefusesWiredAttach`\n55|through the wired attach); B34 discloses reopening before retry;\n56|the README refuses new writable attaches only once the closure\n57|report commits. The rev5 construction (incarnation-scoped proof,\n58|advisory-memory split, writer/reader censuses) stands unchanged\n59|around the bound: the rev4 regressions\n60|(`TestReviewExistingActiveMemoryCannotReopenQuiescedInput`,\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
